  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">National HIV Prevention Program of Sri Lanka - Sri Lanka (01-Jan-2019-31-Dec-2021)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sri Lanka, HIV, The Family Planning Association of Sri Lanka (FPASL)This program has the following goals: Ending AIDS by 2025. The objectives of this program are: To prevent new infections of HIV/STI among key populations, vulnerable populations and the general population.  To provide universal access to HIV/STI diagnosis and treatment, care and support services for those infected and affected by HIV/STI.  To strengthen strategic information systems and knowledge management for an evidence-based response.  To strengthen health systems at different levels and to ensure an effective multi-sector HIV/AIDS/STI response.  To provide a supportive environment for easy access and delivery of HIV prevention, diagnosis, treatment and care services for all</narrative>
  </description>
